Hi David,

The ESP SCSI driver is causing build errors on sparc32 (sun4c) on 
2.6.22-rc6.

   CC      init/version.o
   LD      init/built-in.o
   LD      .tmp_vmlinux1
`scsi_esp_unregister' referenced in section `__ksymtab' of 
drivers/built-in.o: defined in discarded section `.exit.text' of 
drivers/built-in.o
make[1]: *** [.tmp_vmlinux1] Error 1
make: *** [all] Error 2

The fix I am using is to remove the __devexit from line 2352 of 
esp_scsi.c:

--- linux-2.6/drivers/scsi/esp_scsi.c   2007-06-27 15:42:24.000000000 +0100
+++ linux-test/drivers/scsi/esp_scsi.c  2007-06-27 18:13:16.000000000 +0100
@@ -2349,7 +2349,7 @@
  }
  EXPORT_SYMBOL(scsi_esp_register);

-void __devexit scsi_esp_unregister(struct esp *esp)
+void scsi_esp_unregister(struct esp *esp)
  {
  	scsi_remove_host(esp->host);
  }

Is this the correct fix or is there an alternative available?
I have attached the configuration file incase it is a configuration issue.

Regards
 	Mark Fortescue.

